desc:GFX G M1K
//tags: instrument synth poly analogue rack matrix
//author: JGWizrad / Garden FX (GFX)
//
// Requires gfx-drift, gfx-output, gfx-ui, gfx-panel, gfx-instrument, gfx-voice, gfx-dyn and gfx-faceplate
// (.jsfx-inc) in the same folder.
//
// A six-voice analogue rack module in the spirit of the late-80s matrix-modulation synths: a single-space
// box full of patches, with a full editor behind the EDIT key.
// VOICE       two DCOs each: a SAW that morphs to TRIANGLE (SHAPE) and a PULSE (PW), switched in independently;
//             DCO 2 adds NOISE (in place of its waves) and SYNC to DCO 1; MIX balances the two.
//             24 dB low-pass VCF: CUTOFF, RESONANCE, ENV 1 amount, KEY tracking and FM (DCO 1 sweeping the cutoff).
//             VCA 1 = velocity and level; VCA 2 = ENV 2.
//             Three DADSR envelopes (ENV 1 -> VCF, ENV 2 -> VCA, ENV 3 free), two LFOs (LFO 1 -> vibrato,
//             LFO 2 -> pulse width), two RAMPs (rise from zero after each note: delayed vibrato, slow swells).
// MATRIX      five slots: SOURCE x AMOUNT -> DESTINATION.
//             Sources: ENV 1-3, LFO 1-2, RAMP 1-2, VELOCITY, KEYBOARD, MOD WHEEL, AFTERTOUCH.
//             Destinations: DCO 1 / DCO 2 / BOTH pitch (+/-12 st), PW, DCO 1 / 2 SHAPE, MIX, CUTOFF (+/-5 oct),
//             RESONANCE, AMP, FM, VIBRATO depth (+/-100 cents).
// PATCHES     100 factory patches in seven banks (KEYBOARD, STRINGS, WIND+PERC, SYNTH, BASS, LEAD, EFFECTS).
//             Choosing a patch loads every voice setting (your edits stay until you choose another patch -
//             save them as a Reaper preset).
// PLAY        POLY (6 voices), MONO (legato, last note) or UNISON (all six voices on one note, spread).
//             GLIDE, VELOCITY, BEND range, VOLUME, MIDI channel.
// DRIFT (GFX instrument standard): the tuning wanders, each voice's DCOs drift apart in fine pitch and pulse
//             width, the filter breathes, and every note lands slightly differently in tune.
// MIDI: pitch bend, CC1 mod wheel, channel aftertouch, CC64 sustain, CC123 all notes off.
// FACEPLATE   black (the early boxes) or cream (the 90s boxes): the key beside the display swaps them.

import gfx-drift.jsfx-inc
import gfx-output.jsfx-inc
import gfx-ui.jsfx-inc
import gfx-panel.jsfx-inc
import gfx-instrument.jsfx-inc
import gfx-voice.jsfx-inc
import gfx-dyn.jsfx-inc
import gfx-faceplate.jsfx-inc

slider1:0<0,99,1>-Patch
slider2:0<-24,6,0.1>-Volume (dB)
slider3:25<0,100,1>-Drift (%)
slider4:0<0,16,1>-MIDI channel (0 = omni)
